{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template","id":972154,"title":"Unihar as a minor template","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-18T15:16:23-07:00","id":972154,"title":"Unihar as a minor template","content":"I know, I know some of you are thinking, not the unihar again. I wasn't a big fan of them either. But then I remembered a conversation I had a while ago with my friend about minor templates and how great they are. <br /> <br /> So a while back my friend and I were discussing how great the minor templates are and how they help to develop your character through the game and evolve them into amazing characters. We discussed the minor templates of V:tR, M:tA, and W:tF. However, when he asked me if there are other minor templates in W:tF besides the Wolf Blooded I told him no. Then he asked me about the Unihar. I reminded him again that it was taken out. Then he asks, why couldn't it be turned into a minor template without the whole taboo (which we are thankful that it has been removed). I thought about it and asked him how will they fit into the game? He said, they will be a special type of wolf blooded who are pure breeds like in 1ed without the dumb taboo and monstrous child. I told him wolf blooded already have that. His point basically was to make the unihar a minor template equal to revenants and proximi, which wasn't bad and I actually like it. Reminds me of &quot;Being Human&quot; U.S. version with the pure breed twins. Unfortunately we haven't had any time to work on it because of school and work. I was wondering if you guys can help me out.<br /> <br /> So far I've been asking myself questions on how they will fit into werewolf society, what type of powers or abilities will they have, and what effects or specials can they do and etc.. I looked at revenants and proximi and both can use the same source power as their major templates (vitae and mana). The unihar will have primal urge 0 and can store and use essence. As for their powers I'm not quite sure... They can't use gifts because it requires renown so how about dread powers? I was also thinking maybe they can shapeshift into some of the 5 forms, say...2 or 3 forms only including their benefits. Creating a unihar is the same as creating a wolf blooded except without integrity and tells. So far this is what I have come up and currently I'm trying to figure out the negative aspects of being a unihar, if there's any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:39:20-07:00","id":972173,"title":"","content":"Some people seem to have an issue with the whole Shadow or magic part of the game.<br /> <br /> Why not just let them have full shapeshifting at Harmony 9, or 8 if you want them to be able to shift at will. Completely bar the Hisil and spirits, including lunes and Renown and Auspice, from them. They have the bane of silver, no Gifts, the Primal Urge benefits without the sacred hunt penalty or Essence, so their regeneration just does bashing unless they're in Kuruth.<br /> <br /> Basically a more classic movie werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:39:34-07:00","id":972198,"title":"","content":"I sometimes keep forgetting that all minor templates have integrity. I guess harmony 9 wouldn't work. I'm still not sure if giving them access to all 5 forms would be good. Would it make them a little overpowered as a minor template? Yeah, the rest could work. I was thinking they could have some kind of power like revenants have disciplines and proximi have blessings. Of course they can't use gifts but maybe dread powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:57:38-07:00","id":972211,"title":"","content":"I just meant the equivalent of Harmony 9 or 8, in terms of ability to shapechange and Kuruth. They could still have Integrity.<br /> <br /> It would make them pretty powerful but a ghoul can learn every Discipline there is and that's pretty tough too, revenants can learn every non-Clan specific Discipline. If you want you could just narrow it down to human, gauru, urhan. Or human, gauru, urshul. Or just human and another. But when you limit it to just one form you may as well be using a wolf-blooded, as there's Tells that allow you to shift to one form. Even if you're limiting it to two, then you could just have two of those Tells.<br /> <br /> Boiled down, it's a shifting of Attributes and Traits and some increased healing and senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:37:19-07:00","id":972230,"title":"","content":"Yeah, three forms sound good. I'll probably stick to hishu, dalu, and urhan. <br /> <br /> For primal urge benefits they can store and use essence for healing and use of dread powers, which I think I will stick to. Though I wonder what will happen once they run out of essence. Will they go into rage, wasu-im until they regain essence, go into a coma until someone gives them essence, or simply nothing. I always wondered that for werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:18:43-07:00","id":972251,"title":"","content":"What about rites and numina instead of dread powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:44:02-07:00","id":972260,"title":"","content":"Numina is more of a ephemeral spirit type power, which I don't see the Unihar as. If anything dread power is more flesh and spirit. Well since the unihar can use essence they can also use rites too. I see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:46:49-07:00","id":972261,"title":"","content":"Why can't they use Gifts, with something else (like half Willpower, or some Attribute mapped to each Renown) in place of Renown? Proximi don't technically have Gnosis or Arcana - they just roll Willpower. Why not these?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:13:13-07:00","id":972277,"title":"","content":"I think they should be able to earn renown and gifts, but not start with any at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template#post972154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far I've been asking myself questions on how they will fit into werewolf society, (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as their place in society...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The gray wolf is a social animal, whose basic social unit consists of a mated pair, accompanied by the pair's adult offspring.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gray_wolf#cite_note-57\" target=\"_blank\">[c]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The average </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pack_(canine)\" target=\"_blank\">pack</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> consists of a family of 5\u201311 animals (1\u20132 adults, 3\u20136 juveniles and 1\u20133 yearlings),</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gray_wolf#cite_note-heptner1998-11\" target=\"_blank\">[9]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> or sometimes two or three such families,</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gray_wolf#cite_note-paquet2003-4\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> with exceptionally large packs consisting of 42 wolves being known.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gray_wolf#cite_note-m2-58\" target=\"_blank\">[55]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> In ideal conditions, the mated pair produces pups every year, with such offspring typically staying in the pack for 10\u201354 months before dispersing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that it would be a great way to tell stories about &quot;mated pairs&quot; and their children, protecting them and such. These pairs could then form alliances. You can get pretty big and complicated packs that result from werewolves, unihar, wolfblood, and humans all involved in big family networks which make up packs. The main conflict is that the Werewolves with Unihar children may consider the needs of their children's above others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T22:13:39-07:00","id":972351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template?p=972261#post972261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't they use Gifts, with something else (like half Willpower, or some Attribute mapped to each Renown) in place of Renown? Proximi don't technically have Gnosis or Arcana - they just roll Willpower. Why not these?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about this over dinner and it would make sense for them to use gifts. I wanted this at first but in order to use gifts you need renown, which allows werewolves to use and learn gifts. I didn't want to give the unihar renown because I feel it will be too close to their major template and because renown seem something like the uratha should only have. So I thought about it and decided why not give them something that mimics renown like &quot;brands or marks&quot;. The unihar will get two marks (cunning, glory, honor, purity, wisdom) from their parent's auspice renown during their time of birth. Or gain a mark during the lunar phase they were born. And once they go through the first change the mark(s) they had will be put into their renown. Can they gain other &quot;brands or marks&quot;? I'm not sure yet.... This is just something I'm throwing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T22:23:09-07:00","id":972356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template?p=972277#post972277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they should be able to earn renown and gifts, but not start with any at all. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as their place in society...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would argue that it would be a great way to tell stories about &amp;quot;mated pairs&amp;quot; and their children, protecting them and such. These pairs could then form alliances. You can get pretty big and complicated packs that result from werewolves, unihar, wolfblood, and humans all involved in big family networks which make up packs. The main conflict is that the Werewolves with Unihar children may consider the needs of their children's above others.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds more like the Ivory Claws might do since family is a big thing for them. I can imagine that instead of wolf blooded they might have unihar. But I get what your saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:47:10-07:00","id":972487,"title":"","content":"Read The Pack, they have a Pack Merit that allows Wolf-Blooded to earn Renown and learn Gifts. Exactly what you need to put them on par with Proximi and Ghouls. The new merits combined with Tells allows for a Minor Template with pretty solid places to grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:14:59-07:00","id":972499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template?p=972277#post972277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they should be able to earn renown and gifts, but not start with any at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you wanted to wrap it back around to the &quot;Unihar = bad&quot;, you could give them a nice, easy, optional way to quickly gain Renown: they get their parents' Renown if/when they kill them. Nothing <i>forces</i> them to be patri/matri-cidal, but the incentive is there, so that <i>some</i> bad rep or stigma about Unihar is justified.<br /> <br /> EDIT: An a scene regarding gaming the (proposed) system occurred to me: A parent is dying, and they ask the Unihar/child to be the one to end them, so as to pass on their power/Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-19-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:43:48-07:00","id":972912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template?p=972487#post972487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read The Pack, they have a Pack Merit that allows Wolf-Blooded to earn Renown and learn Gifts. Exactly what you need to put them on par with Proximi and Ghouls. The new merits combined with Tells allows for a Minor Template with pretty solid places to grow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's awesome! I got The Pack a few days ago, though I haven't finished reading it. I'll check it out and see what I can come up. Thanks dude!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:51:05-07:00","id":972915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template?p=972499#post972499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if you wanted to wrap it back around to the &amp;quot;Unihar = bad&amp;quot;, you could give them a nice, easy, optional way to quickly gain Renown: they get their parents' Renown if/when they kill them. Nothing <i>forces</i> them to be patri/matri-cidal, but the incentive is there, so that <i>some</i> bad rep or stigma about Unihar is justified.<br /> <br /> EDIT: An a scene regarding gaming the (proposed) system occurred to me: A parent is dying, and they ask the Unihar/child to be the one to end them, so as to pass on their power/Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, the Pure will definitely hate them and the Ivory Claws will be conflicted. This will make them a big fat reminder of Father Wolf's death. Overall I think they will be look down upon in werewolf society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:17:12-07:00","id":973121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/972154-unihar-as-a-minor-template?p=972915#post972915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, the Pure will definitely hate them and the Ivory Claws will be conflicted. This will make them a big fat reminder of Father Wolf's death. Overall I think they will be look down upon in werewolf society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right! There would be <i>some</i> reason, even if it is a gross exaggeration. Most probably wouldn't murder their parents for power. But they <i>could</i>. That's bound to make them interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:35:33-07:00","id":998270,"title":"","content":"So is this dead, or...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:12:53-08:00","id":999253,"title":"","content":"Sorry dude I've been really busy. I have been tinkering with it and so far I'm going to stick brands so it can gain renown to use certain gifts. I'll try to see if I can post the rest of what I have come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T13:55:25-08:00","id":1003045,"title":"","content":"So, what I've got so far as a general Minor+ Template (inspired largely on what is in this thread):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Build a Wolf-Blooded Character</li> <li>Add an additional Tell (gives a bit more flexibility with how Werewolf-y you want them)</li> <li>Add an Essence pool of 5 (can spend 1 per Turn)</li> <li>Primal Urge is effectively 1 for when it matters (but they don't have a &quot;real&quot; Primal Urge)</li> <li>[Healing at half Primal Urge 1 - 1 Bashing every 2 Turns, 1 Lethal every 30 minutes]</li> <li>Add 2 Renown (as determined by their parents' Auspices, or highest Renown).<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Renown brands take physical (not merely spiritual) form as birthmarks, scars, etc.</li> <li>Can acquire additional Renown, but lacking affinities, survivability, or easy access to the Shadow, it is harder.</li> <li>Can acquire parent's Renown by killing them.</li> </ol></li> <li>Add 1 Shadow Gift<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can acquire additional Shadow Gifts from spirits normally (barring the <i>Siskur Dah</i>), except the wounds inflicted are 1 Aggravated, not 1 Lethal.</li> <li>[Can acquire parent's Shadow Gifts by killing them]</li> </ol></li> <li>[Add 1 Wolf Gift OR Can acquire Wolf Gifts]<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can acquire them normally.</li> <li>[If a Wolf Gift modifies a Form, it instead grants access to that modified Form. Use Integrity as Harmony, if Integrity is used]</li> </ol></li> <li>Can learn/use Wolf Rites</li> <li>[Add Spirit Senses]</li> <li>[Use Harmony?]</li> </ol>[] = Uncertain about inclusion<br /> <br /> In this model, Unihar are Wolf-Blooded with 1 more Tell, a small Essence Pool, and access to Renown/Most Gifts and Wolf Rites. Optional inclusion is minor Regeneration, Spirit Senses, and maybe Harmony instead of Integrity. Regen and Spirit Senses could be approximated by Tells. They lack inherent Form changing abilities (but some Tells can grant that, and optionally The Father 's Form might unlock a kind of Gauru), Auspices (since they haven't actually underwent a First Change yet), Moon Gifts (again, no First Change), or Gift Affinities (no Auspice and aren't werewolves). The &quot;get parent's stuff by killing them&quot; calls back to the 1E material and gives them a bad reputation, but nothing forces them to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}